<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="Test3">
  <title>Chapter 2 </title>
  
  <section xml:id="sec-test3">
    <title>Investigations into Sage 3D plots</title>
    <p>
      Below is a set of plots used to test how different Sage plots will be rendered. 
    </p>
    <p>
      Here is a plot with the 3d variant of sageplot that uses threejs as a render. 
    </p>
    <figure xml:id="fig123">
      <caption>Caption goes here</caption>
      <image>
        <description><p>Description goes here</p></description>
        <sageplot variant="3d" label="interact-fig123">
          var('s,t')
          P0=(-1/2,-1/2,0)
          P1=(1/2,-1/2,0)
          P2=(-1/2,1/2,0)
          d=1.5
          plot9=parametric_plot3d((s,-s/3+t,0),(s,-d,d),(t,-d,d),color="lightblue",mesh=True,plot_points=4,frame=False,opacity=0.5)
          plot9+=arrow(P0,P1,color="blue")+arrow(P0,P2,color="blue")+arrow(P0,(-1/2,-1/2,1.5),color="red")
          plot9+=point(P0,size=30,color="black")+point(P1,size=30,color="black")+point(P2,size=30,color="black")
          plot9+=text3d("P\u2080",(-.75,-0.85,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)+text3d("P\u2081",(1,-0.45,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
          plot9+=text3d("P\u2082",(-.75,0.75,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
          plot9+=arrow(P0,(1,1,0),color="blue")+text3d("P",(1.1,1.3,0.15),color="black",fontsize=25)+point3d((1,1,0),color="black",size=30)
          plot9+=text3d("n",(-0.5,-0.5,2),color="red",fontsize=25,viewpoint=[[-0.905,-0.2098,-0.37],64.14],camera_position=[3.7891,-4.5159,3.2116])
          plot9
        </sageplot>
      </image>
    </figure>
    <program language="sage$">
      <input>
        var('s,t')
        P0=(-1/2,-1/2,0)
        P1=(1/2,-1/2,0)
        P2=(-1/2,1/2,0)
        d=1.5
        plot9=parametric_plot3d((s,-s/3+t,0),(s,-d,d),(t,-d,d),color="lightblue",mesh=True,plot_points=4,frame=False,opacity=0.5)
        plot9+=arrow(P0,P1,color="blue")+arrow(P0,P2,color="blue")+arrow(P0,(-1/2,-1/2,1.5),color="red")
        plot9+=point(P0,size=30,color="black")+point(P1,size=30,color="black")+point(P2,size=30,color="black")
        plot9+=text3d("P\u2080",(-.75,-0.85,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)+text3d("P\u2081",(1,-0.45,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
        plot9+=text3d("P\u2082",(-.75,0.75,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
        plot9+=arrow(P0,(1,1,0),color="blue")+text3d("P",(1.1,1.3,0.15),color="black",fontsize=25)+point3d((1,1,0),color="black",size=30)
        plot9+=text3d("n",(-0.5,-0.5,2),color="red",fontsize=25,viewpoint=[[-0.905,-0.2098,-0.37],64.14],camera_position=[3.0163,-6.0448,3.4513])
        plot9
      </input>
    </program>
    <p>
      The issues here are that we can't seem to specify the camera location to get the zoom and framing correct as they need to appear on the webpage. For instance, the plot shown above is not centered as we would want on the plane. Would like to know how to specify the viewpoint/camera_position/zoom to specify exactly how we want the initial plot to look on the webpage (and dead tree page eventually).
    </p>
    <p>
      Which leads to the next want. Specifically, how to pass other options to the .save command to get better screenshots of 3D plots.
    </p>
    <program language="sage$">
      <input>
        var('s,t')
        P0=(-1/2,-1/2,0)
        P1=(1/2,-1/2,0)
        P2=(-1/2,1/2,0)
        d=1.5
        plot9=parametric_plot3d((s,-s/3+t,0),(s,-d,d),(t,-d,d),color="lightblue",mesh=True,plot_points=4,frame=False,opacity=0.5)
        plot9+=arrow(P0,P1,color="blue")+arrow(P0,P2,color="blue")+arrow(P0,(-1/2,-1/2,1.5),color="red")
        plot9+=point(P0,size=30,color="black")+point(P1,size=30,color="black")+point(P2,size=30,color="black")
        plot9+=text3d("P\u2080",(-.75,-0.85,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)+text3d("P\u2081",(1,-0.45,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
        plot9+=text3d("P\u2082",(-.75,0.75,0.35),color="black",fontsize=25)
        plot9+=arrow(P0,(1,1,0),color="blue")+text3d("P",(1.1,1.3,0.15),color="black",fontsize=25)+point3d((1,1,0),color="black",size=30)
        plot9+=text3d("n",(-0.5,-0.5,2),color="red",fontsize=25,viewpoint=[[-0.905,-0.2098,-0.37],64.14],camera_position=[3.7891,-4.5159,3.2116])
        plot9.save("planewith3points.png",viewer="threejs")
      </input>
    </program>
    <p>
      This yields the following image. 
    </p>
    <image source="./planewith3points.png"/>
    <p>
      Which is not good. Is there way to get a better screenshot (like with the save as png option through the threejs menu on an interactive graphic, as shown below).
    </p>
    <image source="./threejs_screenshot.png"/>
  </section>
</chapter>
